NOT A MEDICAL DEVICE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The Apache License's "AS IS" clause disclaims warranty. It says nothing about
clinical use, so this does:

This software is a research and training prototype for use by REGISTERED
CLINICIANS. It is not a medical device, it has not been clinically validated,
it has not been submitted to or approved by any regulatory authority, and it
must not be used for patient-facing decisions or as a substitute for clinical
judgement.

Its own generated reports carry machine-authored warnings naming what could not
be verified. Those warnings are part of the output, not decoration: every
recommendation must be checked against the cited source document, at the cited
page, before any action is taken. The drug recommendation path in particular is
documented in README section "Why indication support is deliberately
conservative" as NOT usable prescribing output.


